- `rtk cargo fmt --all --check`
- `rtk git diff --check`

## Outcomes

- Fetch no longer sleeps for `max_wait_ms` after a response already satisfies `min_bytes`.
- Fetch byte accounting now uses each poll attempt's response bytes, rather than accumulating bytes across retries.
- Fetch caps storage reads per partition by `partition_max_bytes` and spends global `max_bytes` only on retained batches.
- SQLite/libsql broker Fetch was unblocked by removing PostgreSQL-style casts from `producer_select_for_update.sql`, which had broken idempotent produce setup for Fetch tests.
- Compatibility contract and all-target check passed; API 1 remains routed but unadvertised and semantically uncertified.

## Residual Risks

- API 23 remains unadvertised until differential/client proof.
- Leader epoch truncation/recovery and read-committed transaction integration remain unproven.
- Fetch incremental sessions, topic ID behavior, broader max-bytes parity, and Java/librdkafka seek proof remain open.

